## Development Task

```
mysql> drop table if exists t1, t2;
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.03 sec)

mysql> create table t1(a int, b varchar(8));
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.02 sec)

mysql> insert into t1 values(1,'1');
Query OK, 1 row affected (0.00 sec)

mysql> create table t2(a int , b varchar(8) GENERATED ALWAYS AS (c) VIRTUAL, c varchar(8), PRIMARY KEY (a));
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.01 sec)

mysql> insert into t2(a) values(1);
Query OK, 1 row affected (0.00 sec)

mysql> SELECT /*+ tidb_inlj(t2) */ t2.b, t1.b from t1 join t2 ON t2.a=t1.a;
ERROR 1105 (HY000): inner child of Projection should be IndexLookupReader, but got *core.PhysicalProjection
```

Currently, in `buildProjectionForIndexJoin`, we make an assertion that if the root operator of index join's inner child is Projection, its child must be a `IndexLookUp`. However, in planner we do not enforce this constraint when building index join plans. We should either do this check in planner, or support `TableReader` / `IndexReader` as child of inner Projection in executor. I prefer the latter one.
